## 3. Data Source

| Attribute | Detail |
|---|---|
| **Dataset** | `manufacturing_b2b_dataset.xlsx` |
| **Key Columns** | `Client_Review`, `Review_Sentiment`, `Rating`, `Client_Name` |
| **Size** | 500+ real B2B client reviews |
| **Data Type** | Mixed — free-text reviews + structured metadata |

---

## 4. Constraints

- Model must be lightweight and run on a local machine — **no dedicated GPU required**
- Minimum acceptable accuracy: **> 85%** for business deployment
- Must handle real-world noisy text (typos, informal phrasing, mixed languages)
- Output must be presented as a **business-friendly dashboard**, not raw model metrics

---

## 5. Success Criteria

| Criterion | Result | Target | Status |
|---|---|---|---|
| Model Accuracy | 100% (Weighted Precision/Recall/F1 = 1.00) | > 85% | ✅ Exceeded |
| Business Dashboard | 54.8% Positive / 45.2% Negative | Actionable insight | ✅ Delivered |
| Functionality | Sentiment classification, fake-review flagging, downloadable report | Core features working | ✅ Complete |

> **Note for review:** A 100% accuracy score on a ~500-row dataset is worth double-checking before final submission — it can be a genuine result on a clean, well-separated dataset, but it's also a common symptom of test-data leakage or an overly small/simple test split. Worth confirming the train/test split was done correctly (no shared rows, stratified split) before presenting this number as final.

---

## 6. Tech Stack

- **Language:** Python
- **Data Handling:** Pandas
- **Modeling:** Scikit-learn — TF-IDF Vectorizer + Logistic Regression
- **NLP:** Text cleaning and preprocessing pipeline

